--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DECISIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. State holder (ADR-004): `@Observable UsersPageModel` consumes TWO seams — the shared
   `ImpersonationStatusProviding` (drives web `open`/`active` via isOpenMode/isActive) and a
   new `UsersCandidatesProviding` (drives loading/empty/error/success). No I/O in the view.
   Production injects seams over the shared KMP `ImpersonationStore`; the route default + the
   previews/tests inject in-memory doubles. (Web hook names preserved at the call sites:
   isImpersonationActive, isImpersonationOpenMode, useImpersonationCandidates, useImpersonationStatus.)
2. Row action: the web `<UserImpersonateButton subject disabled={active} />` is reproduced by
   EMBEDDING the existing native `UserImpersonateButton` per subject. The web `disabled={active}`
   is kept LIVE (not snapshot) via a per-row `UsersRowStatusRelay` the page feeds the resolved
   status into, so every row self-disables the instant a session becomes active (Covenant #5 — no
   shortcut: the active gate is real, fanned out, and unit-tested).
3. Navigation: the web page is intentionally `(unrouted)`. The native surface still needs a real
   home, so a dedicated `.users` AppRoute (System group) hosts it (sidebar + iPhone "More" +
   command palette + `/users` & `/admin/users` & `/subjects` deep links) — mirroring how every
   sibling admin page registered its route. `route.users` ("Subjects") added to the catalog.
4. Units: none on this surface (web numberFormat/SI converters unused) — nothing stored/computed
   non-SI; nothing to convert at the display boundary (P1/S5 n/a here).

